# No spelling rules for this language yet.

# find-accent-misspellings.py: ä and ö are letters of their own, so a plain
# spelling is often another word (vaara/väärä, saari/sääri).
no-misspellings

# find-supplement.py: Common Voice has little Finnish text (35k words), so
# a word form seen this many times in Common Voice and Tatoeba together is
# enough (a noun has hundreds of forms; most are rare in any corpus).
one-source 3

# Word forms the list lacks (dictionary.h: isWordForm): typed, they stand;
# they are never suggested. Clitics attach to any form (onko, tuletkin),
# -s and the possessives only after a vowel; a possessive replaces a final
# n or t (talon, talot -> taloni). Up to two endings (talossanikin).
suffix kaan kään kin han hän ko kö pa pä
suffix s after=aeiouyäö
suffix ni si mme nne nsa nsä after=aeiouyäö drop=nt
# Compounds: up to three words of at least four letters (parkki+paikkaa),
# and hyphenated parts (juna-asemalta).
compound 4 3
